$$ cdb first-chance access-violation capture for Smatchet.
$$ Breaks BEFORE the app's frame-loop SEH filter swallows the AV, so you get the PRIMARY
$$ faulting stack (the real use-after-free / null deref), not the std::exit->terminate tail.
$$
$$ Usage (run cdb from the build dir so the app resolves Scripts/):
$$   cdb -y "<build-dir>;srv*C:\Tools\symcache*https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols" \
$$       -cf scripts\dev\av-capture.cdb <path-to>\Smatchet.exe
$$ Then reproduce; on the first AV it prints the faulting + all-thread stacks, writes a full
$$ dump, and quits. Get cdb by extracting it from the WinDbg msixbundle (https://aka.ms/windbg/download).
.lines -e
.symopt+0x10
.echo SMATCHET_CDB_ARMED
sxe -c ".echo ===SMATCHET_AV_HIT===; .exr -1; .echo ---FAULTING-THREAD---; kP 120; .echo ---ALL-THREADS---; ~*kb 40; .dump /ma ${env:LOCALAPPDATA}\CrashDumps\smatchet_av_firstchance.dmp; .echo ===SMATCHET_AV_CAPTURED===; q" av
g
